**Given:**

Radius of the circle with center O (r₁) = 49 cm.

Radius of the circle with center A (r₂) = 16 cm.

**Formula used:**

Length of the common tangent = sqrt{d²-(r₁ -r₂)²}

Where, d = distance between centre

**Calculation:**

Distance between centre = 49 + 16 = 65

So,

Length of the common tangent 

⇒ sqrt{65²-(49 -16)²} 

⇒ sqrt{65²-33²} 

⇒ sqrt{(65+33)(65-33)}

⇒ sqrt{98× 32} 

⇒ sqrt{98× 2×16} 

⇒ 7 × 2 × 4 = 56 cm

**∴ The correct answer is option (4).**

